  "configuration_id": "config_007",
  "reason": "Evidence: The scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile space is fully explored (all 4 aggregation/fusion combos tested), with config_024 (transformer+weighted) as the best at 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1. The only major untested design axis for scvi_n200 is the image encoder. For scgpt, resnet50 was ~3-4 points worse than imagenet_vit_l, but the interaction with scvi_n200 is unknown. Question: Does config_007 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + weighted) — the direct image-encoder swap of our best config — achieve comparable accuracy? This clarifies whether imagenet_vit_l is essential or whether resnet50 is a sufficient, potentially cheaper alternative. Rationale: With only 1 experiment remaining after this, testing the most impactful unexplored variable (image encoder) for the dominant RNA encoder is the highest-information experiment. If resnet50 is within ~1 point of vit_l, it confirms cost-effectiveness; if it lags significantly, it validates config_024 as the optimal choice. Expected cost: moderate, estimated ~3.5–5 GPU hours (resnet50 is architecturally lighter than ViT-L, though the scgpt comparison showed variable overhead; comparable to other scvi_n200 multiprofile runs at 3.6–4.8 hrs)."
}

